Subject: Re: Onboarding: Streaming + Tool Calls + Structured Output (Next Steps)

Hi Laura / Arvind —

Quick answers and an inline minimal schema to use in the kickoff:

1) Minimal JSON schema (example) you can drop into your validator and also pass as the structured_output.schema when calling our API:

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "diagnostic_summary": {"type": "string"},
    "confidence_score": {"type": "number"},
    "metrics": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "latency_ms": {"type": "number"},
        "tokens_generated": {"type": "integer"}
      }
    }
  },
  "required": ["diagnostic_summary"]
}

2) Function / tool-calls: sample event we emit when the model invokes a tool:
- tool_call.name: "lookup_patient_record"
- tool_call.args: JSON object (string) that is passed to your tool endpoint
- We recommend idempotent tool endpoints. On 5xx, Redwood will retry once immediately and surface the failure in the response payload; if you want a different retry policy we can configure an exponential backoff at the routing layer.

3) Streaming specifics: use the streaming endpoint with the query param "stream=true"; the server will emit SSE-like chunks where each chunk contains either a partial token frame or a final structured_output block. To minimize reassembly complexity, ask for a final JSON object under the key "structured_output" and include a top-level "schema_version". Example final frame: {
  "structured_output": { /* matches schema */ },
  "schema_version": "v1"
}

4) Sandbox / allowlist: send IPs to infra-team@redwood.ai (cc Monica). For initial sandbox we provide a short-lived API key with role: "sandbox_integration".

I attached json-schema-example.json and will bring a sample streaming trace to the call.

—Dev
Principal Engineer, Redwood Inference
